    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0398" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1914-20v02/pg352"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/1047½</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">President Wilson to the Counselor for the Department of
                        State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Polk</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-28">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">28 January, 1918</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Counselor</hi>: Thank you for the
                        enclosed.<anchor n="36" xml:id="d182-f1"/> I dare say that for the present
                    we may let this matter stand as it does; but I hope that we shall soon have new
                    material for judgment in the shape of further information from our Ambassador at
                    Tokyo. I do not think that it will be safe or wise to leave the Japanese
                    government in any doubt as to the impression such an attitude on their part
                    makes on us.</p>
                <p>Faithfully Yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>W. W.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
